     {
      "text": "72-year-old male presenting with excessive thirst and frequent urination for 1 weeks. Character: passing urine many times, also at night; radiation: n/a; aggravated by sweet food; relieved by nothing. Severity 2/10. Associated: weight loss, blurred vision. PMH: Type 2 diabetes for 7 years; Hypertension for 5 years. Drugs: Metformin 500 mg; Amlodipine 5 mg. Allergy: dust. Family: diabetes. Personal: occasional alcohol. Triage: ROUTINE."
